Come over

04:16.190 --> 04:16.270
I'm on a walk with 
Osanai-san. Later

04:16.190 --> 04:16.270
No problem.
Bring her with you

04:16.270 --> 04:18.360
Come over

04:16.270 --> 04:18.360
I'm on a walk with 
Osanai-san. Later

04:16.270 --> 04:18.360
No problem.
Bring her with you

04:18.540 --> 04:19.560
Hold up a second.

04:21.650 --> 04:24.290
Kengo's asking if I want to come over.

04:25.460 --> 04:26.910
Really?

04:27.430 --> 04:28.760
Okay, see you.

04:28.760 --> 04:32.480
No, he asked if you wanted to come, too.

04:32.480 --> 04:33.750
Me, too?

04:38.250 --> 04:39.210
Thanks for waiting.

04:40.680 --> 04:42.130
Disguise removed.

04:42.470 --> 04:43.350
Hm?

04:43.350 --> 04:45.210
Nothing. Let's go.

04:55.770 --> 04:57.310
Oh, you're here.

04:58.640 --> 05:00.110
Hi, Osanai-san.

05:00.760 --> 05:02.030
Hello.

05:02.030 --> 05:03.180
Well, come in.

05:09.380 --> 05:11.600
Oh, here. Cakes.

05:11.600 --> 05:13.610
We didn't want to come empty-handed.

05:12.700 --> 05:14.830
<b>Keep refrigerated</b>

05:15.140 --> 05:16.090
Huh?

05:18.080 --> 05:21.360
It was actually Osanai-san's idea.

05:23.540 --> 05:25.940
Yeah, I figured. Thanks.

05:26.480 --> 05:27.420
Not at all.

05:29.000 --> 05:31.570
I'll be right back. 
I have some nice hot cocoa.

05:32.000 --> 05:34.110
You can get started on the cakes.

05:38.310 --> 05:39.930
Which one should I have?

05:48.540 --> 05:50.790
Kengo, do you want to take that cake?

05:50.790 --> 05:52.420
Sure, I'll have whatever.

06:03.770 --> 06:05.210
Wow.

06:09.080 --> 06:12.630
You stirred the cocoa powder
 into hot milk, right?

06:12.630 --> 06:13.780
Of course.

06:14.180 --> 06:17.360
It's well-mixed. 
It's not easy to make it like this.

06:17.730 --> 06:18.600
You get it, huh?

06:19.500 --> 06:21.420
I can teach you the trick, if you want.

06:21.420 --> 06:22.950
No, it's fine.

06:22.950 --> 06:27.100
Just hear me out. There's one small trick 
that makes it taste entirely different.

06:27.370 --> 06:30.080
First, you put cocoa powder in the cup.

06:30.080 --> 06:33.160
Then, you pour steaming hot milk on top.

06:33.160 --> 06:37.280
The trick is to start 
with just a little milk.

06:37.590 --> 06:38.750
Huh.

06:38.750 --> 06:45.560
You give it just enough milk 
so that you can knead it into a paste.

06:46.370 --> 06:51.700
Then, once the powder's completely dissolved 
into the paste, you add more hot milk.

06:51.700 --> 06:52.860
As much as you want.

06:53.670 --> 06:55.360
Sugar to taste.

06:55.360 --> 06:59.200
And then, stir some more,
 and there you go.

06:59.740 --> 07:03.050
Man, that's great information.

07:03.050 --> 07:04.020
Thanks.

07:04.460 --> 07:07.500
That one extra step 
really does make a difference.

07:08.340 --> 07:09.590
So, Jogoro...

07:18.220 --> 07:19.290
Um...

07:19.290 --> 07:21.780
May I use the bathroom?

07:21.790 --> 07:27.060
Sure. Take a right over there
 and the door's on the left.

07:27.060 --> 07:28.140
Got that?

07:28.580 --> 07:30.210
I think so.

07:34.740 --> 07:39.950
Well? There must be a reason for
you inviting me over on a Sunday.

07:41.060 --> 07:44.710
Not really. Not anything in particular.

07:44.710 --> 07:49.040
So you're telling me you interrupted 
my walk to give me a lecture

07:49.040 --> 07:51.030
on how to make nice hot cocoa?

07:51.740 --> 07:55.850
I can't quite say I appreciate it,

07:56.240 --> 08:00.290
though I do look forward to 
having nice hot cocoa from now on.

08:01.680 --> 08:05.010
You don't seem to have lost your edge at all.

08:05.870 --> 08:09.370
I'll get to the point. Did something 
happen to you in middle school?

08:09.870 --> 08:15.220
You seem too different. Where'd the
 seemingly invincible Kobato Jogoro go?

08:16.080 --> 08:17.220
For example?

08:17.550 --> 08:21.010
"For example," what? 
I'm talking about everything about you.

08:21.010 --> 08:22.380
Like just now.

08:22.880 --> 08:25.270
I tell you how to make nice hot cocoa,

08:25.270 --> 08:28.310
and you respond with,
 "That's great information. Thanks."

08:31.180 --> 08:35.150
I don't know. How was I before?

08:35.150 --> 08:38.630
You couldn't help sharing
everything you knew.

08:39.080 --> 08:43.470
If someone knew something you didn't, 
you'd get snarky and cry sour grapes.

08:43.950 --> 08:47.350
But you're even worse now.

08:47.850 --> 08:50.050
You're like a nasty little brat

08:50.050 --> 08:54.080
who smiles on the outside, but who you 
suspect has a chip on his shoulder.

08:54.730 --> 08:56.390
So to sum up your question,

08:56.790 --> 09:01.880
you want to know if something 
happened to me at middle school.

09:02.450 --> 09:04.170
Is that what you want to ask?

09:04.170 --> 09:05.860
That would be my question.

09:08.400 --> 09:09.860
That's simple, then.

09:09.860 --> 09:11.560
Nothing happened.

09:11.560 --> 09:16.070
I might have been how you say 
when I first entered middle school.

09:16.070 --> 09:19.290
But I ended up like this naturally 
by the time I graduated.

09:19.590 --> 09:21.300
An ordinary person.

09:21.300 --> 09:22.540
I don't believe it.

09:23.590 --> 09:25.140
That's your choice.

09:25.140 --> 09:27.520
"A leopard doesn't change its spots."

09:27.520 --> 09:31.010
The Jogoro I knew wouldn't have 
turned out like this for no small reason.

09:31.010 --> 09:35.450
"Those little feet aren't little forever."
 It's been three years.

09:35.450 --> 09:37.750
You just haven't changed <i>enough</i>.

09:40.530 --> 09:46.500
It pisses me off when I hear things like 
"I agree" or "You're right" coming from you.

09:47.360 --> 09:50.080
You don't <i>actually</i> agree.

09:50.600 --> 09:53.200
You'll just have to get used to it, then.

09:54.070 --> 09:55.700
I shouldn't have said it like that.

09:56.440 --> 09:59.240
But you know what I'm trying to get at.

09:59.630 --> 10:02.460
Sure, I do. But you see, Kengo...

10:03.130 --> 10:07.680
I think you're hoping there's a simple 
explanation in the form of some trauma.

10:08.150 --> 10:09.730
It's nothing like that.

10:10.170 --> 10:13.360
I'm not trying to become ordinary 
for any particular reason.

10:13.360 --> 10:16.710
Just like you aren't trying to 
be benevolent for a reason.

10:17.830 --> 10:20.080
Is this why you called me over?

10:20.760 --> 10:22.340
If it is, I'll be...

10:24.990 --> 10:28.430
Oh, I'm gonna use your bathroom.

10:28.430 --> 10:29.590
Go ahead.

10:33.080 --> 10:35.630
But that's too much.

10:35.630 --> 10:37.290
You're right.

10:37.290 --> 10:38.860
Something's not right.

10:38.860 --> 10:40.210
Yeah.

10:41.760 --> 10:44.120
Hello, Chisato-san.

10:45.870 --> 10:48.380
Is that you, Kobato-kun?

10:48.380 --> 10:50.890
Yes. It's been a while.

10:57.410 --> 10:58.830
Is something wrong?

10:58.830 --> 11:03.100
That idiot Kengo is challenging us.

11:09.030 --> 11:10.770
The sink is dry.

11:11.380 --> 11:12.130
Uh-huh.

11:12.130 --> 11:15.420
And the only thing in here is a spoon.

11:15.770 --> 11:18.320
Is something wrong with that?

11:18.320 --> 11:19.640
You're so slow.

11:20.080 --> 11:23.660
Kengo made hot cocoa for you two, didn't he?

11:24.140 --> 11:30.820
If he made it with milk and cocoa, 
there needs to have been a pot here.

11:31.650 --> 11:32.920
He must have washed it.

11:33.260 --> 11:35.770
Like I say, the sink is dry.

11:35.770 --> 11:39.430
He made hot, milky cocoa 
without getting the sink wet.

11:40.090 --> 11:41.650
Can you make any sense of it?

11:42.350 --> 11:43.510
I can't.

11:43.510 --> 11:44.550
Neither can I.

11:44.990 --> 11:46.340
Nor can she.

11:48.590 --> 11:50.180
That bum.

11:51.200 --> 11:54.910
Doesn't it piss you off how that idiot 
Kengo can do something you can't?

11:54.910 --> 11:57.200
That does upset me, yes.

11:57.200 --> 11:58.180
Kobato-kun.

11:58.470 --> 12:02.650
How about we retrace Kengo's steps, then?

12:19.260 --> 12:20.700
It's pretty big.

12:20.700 --> 12:23.710
It's so you can use it for making snacks.

12:23.710 --> 12:25.120
It's also an oven.

12:26.250 --> 12:32.050
So your theory is he might have 
made hot milk using the microwave.

12:33.230 --> 12:35.900
You wouldn't need a pot.

12:35.900 --> 12:39.030
On the other hand, 
you'd need a non-metal container.

12:39.030 --> 12:43.750
He has ceramics and plastics and such here.

12:44.150 --> 12:47.870
And yet, the sink is dry.

12:47.870 --> 12:49.860
It must have been like this, then.

13:16.020 --> 13:18.660
That makes three cups of hot cocoa.

13:18.660 --> 13:22.760
But the cocoa he served to us 
wasn't plain hot cocoa.

13:22.760 --> 13:25.770
Right. It was <i>good</i> hot cocoa.

13:26.050 --> 13:32.300
You'd need cups to put the cocoa paste into
 in addition to the cups with the hot milk.

13:38.640 --> 13:41.300
Looks like you've figured out
 the problem with that.

13:41.300 --> 13:43.020
Get it now?

13:43.020 --> 13:45.920
Kengo, that idiot. How'd he do it?

13:46.650 --> 13:49.920
If he didn't use a bowl of some sort...

13:50.570 --> 13:54.350
If he'd put the milk into cups 
and put them in the microwave,

13:54.350 --> 13:56.650
he would have needed six cups.

13:56.650 --> 13:59.180
No, he'd only need four.

14:00.070 --> 14:07.690
Warm up three cups of milk, 
and use one cup for making the cocoa good.

14:07.690 --> 14:10.260
With the cocoa powder mixed,

14:10.260 --> 14:13.840
you'd have one cup of 
hot cocoa and a free cup.

14:13.840 --> 14:18.120
Do that three times, and you get 
three cups of nice hot cocoa.

14:18.900 --> 14:20.800
That's not it, Kobato-kun.

14:20.800 --> 14:25.200
The spoon would have 
been wet after the first cup.

14:26.440 --> 14:28.770
This is Kengo we're talking about.

14:28.770 --> 14:34.140
I wouldn't put it past him to put the 
wet spoon back into the cocoa powder.

14:34.730 --> 14:37.270
Even if that's not the case,

14:37.270 --> 14:43.020
you'd only need one cup to warm up the milk
 and three cups for kneading the powder.

14:43.020 --> 14:48.320
Heat up the milk and put it in the 
powder cups. Do that three times.

14:49.150 --> 14:53.720
You'd still be using four cups.

14:53.720 --> 14:58.130
But he's only used three.

15:02.440 --> 15:08.070
My suspicion is that this case can be
 solved by reframing the question.

15:09.170 --> 15:11.520
There were two good cups of hot cocoa.

15:15.190 --> 15:19.970
The last one just had 
cocoa powder thrown on top.

15:19.970 --> 15:22.520
It was the normal, powdery hot cocoa.

15:23.090 --> 15:28.670
That way, you get two cups of 
nice hot cocoa and one normal cup.

15:28.670 --> 15:29.940
I see.

15:29.940 --> 15:32.150
No, that can't be it.

15:32.150 --> 15:33.210
Why not?

15:33.720 --> 15:38.740
We each took a cup freely 
from the serving tray.

15:39.200 --> 15:42.450
Kengo wasn't the first, either.

15:42.960 --> 15:47.910
You can make three cups of 
hot cocoa from two cups of hot milk.

15:50.970 --> 15:52.010
Heating

15:50.970 --> 15:53.970
Milk

15:52.300 --> 15:53.300
Heating

15:53.550 --> 15:53.970
Heating

16:11.440 --> 16:15.750
Do this twice to make 
two cups of nice hot cocoa.

16:15.750 --> 16:20.520
And this way, you can make 
nice hot cocoa in three cups.

16:20.860 --> 16:26.160
But this only gets each cup
 66% full at the most.

16:26.780 --> 16:32.420
The cocoa we got was filled to the brim.

16:32.820 --> 16:36.520
Jeez. Why even bring it up if you knew?

16:38.070 --> 16:41.010
Oh, uh, I was just trying to fill the silence.

16:43.110 --> 16:45.130
Oh! I got it!

16:45.130 --> 16:47.560
That's it! The little kid's right!

16:47.560 --> 16:48.900
"Little kid"?

16:48.900 --> 16:53.070
You can make three cups of cocoa
 the way she describes.

16:53.450 --> 16:55.260
Then, it's a matter of portions.

16:55.260 --> 16:58.670
Which means you just need 
to make the cocoa rich at first,

16:58.670 --> 17:01.220
then add more milk after.

17:01.220 --> 17:03.010
That would make it cold.

17:03.010 --> 17:07.330
The cocoa we had was so hot, 
we couldn't drink it immediately.

17:07.910 --> 17:11.100
You could microwave it right after.

17:11.100 --> 17:13.230
Heat up two cups of milk,

17:13.230 --> 17:15.470
separate it into three cups of hot cocoa,

17:15.470 --> 17:17.640
add more milk, and warm it up again.

17:18.160 --> 17:20.000
That's too much work.

17:21.700 --> 17:26.220
I can't accept being more 
inefficient than that idiot Kengo.

17:26.220 --> 17:30.350
Seriously, why is cocoa a powder?

17:32.010 --> 17:37.390
If there were some kind of, say, cocoa paste...

17:40.160 --> 17:42.070
It's cocoa powder.

17:42.350 --> 17:43.700
Plain and simple.

17:48.460 --> 17:50.700
So how is the sink dry?

17:51.680 --> 17:54.790
Did he do the dishes and wipe it bone dry?

17:54.790 --> 17:56.700
But there's still a spoon in there.

17:57.430 --> 18:01.100
We would notice if it had gotten wet.

18:03.730 --> 18:07.290
Here's another way to put it:

18:08.480 --> 18:13.720
To make three cups of nice hot cocoa, 
you need four things to get wet.

18:14.480 --> 18:16.250
What's the fourth thing?

18:17.480 --> 18:20.290
Three cups are wet with hot cocoa.

18:21.710 --> 18:26.990
The last thing would be wet
 if it was washed.

18:30.030 --> 18:31.810
If it wasn't washed...

18:33.000 --> 18:33.960
Chisato-san.

18:33.960 --> 18:34.670
What is it?

18:34.670 --> 18:36.360
Could you please open the fridge?

18:38.510 --> 18:41.120
Could you pick up that milk carton?

18:47.440 --> 18:48.750
It's hot, isn't it?

18:50.580 --> 18:56.160
Kengo put the whole carton of milk 
in the microwave to heat it up.

18:58.650 --> 19:01.660
Heating

18:58.650 --> 19:01.660
Milk

18:58.650 --> 19:01.660
cup

19:04.370 --> 19:07.680
In other words, the fourth wet thing...

19:07.680 --> 19:09.910
was the milk carton itself.

19:10.440 --> 19:13.540
That lazy bastard!

19:15.360 --> 19:16.560
Took you a while.

19:17.330 --> 19:18.320
Osanai-san.

19:19.170 --> 19:21.090
The cake was delicious.

19:21.940 --> 19:23.430
I'm glad to hear it.

19:23.430 --> 19:26.420
I spoke with your sister
for the first time in a while.

19:26.420 --> 19:29.190
My sister? What did you talk about?

19:30.570 --> 19:32.300
She gave me a mystery to solve.

19:32.300 --> 19:33.400
A mystery?

19:33.400 --> 19:35.800
Followed by some idle banter.

19:46.660 --> 19:47.200
How to make delicious hot cocoa

19:51.710 --> 19:55.710
How to make delicious hot cocoa

20:06.230 --> 20:08.970
Kobato-kun, was it?

20:08.970 --> 20:10.710
He's pretty good.

20:11.220 --> 20:14.400
I always thought he was pretty smart,
ever since he was a kid.

20:14.740 --> 20:17.240
And he's grown up quite a bit, too.

20:17.690 --> 20:20.720
He even thought to buy a cake for me.

20:25.660 --> 20:28.210
He's nothing like that.

20:30.900 --> 20:34.580
Hey, Osanai-san, it'll be all right.

20:34.580 --> 20:36.740
I won't do anything like that again.

20:37.610 --> 20:41.350
I just got a bit carried away
 because it's Sunday.

20:42.180 --> 20:44.220
I don't know what you're talking about.

20:45.870 --> 20:48.700
We have a promise.

20:49.140 --> 20:53.900
But our promise doesn't decide 
what kind of person you have to be.

20:56.450 --> 21:00.840
Today, you were like how you were 
the first time I met you.

21:02.180 --> 21:06.900
You could be that Kobato-kun again
if it's more fun for you.

21:07.280 --> 21:09.550
I won't mind.

21:09.550 --> 21:13.050
I've quit playing the detective.
